inline_comments.comment:
The tooltip is populated via `.html(this.escapeHtml(title).replace(...))`, which uses a custom hand-rolled escape function. `flowDb.ts` uses the established safer pattern: call `.text()` (letting D3 encode all entities), then read back `.html()` to substitute `<br/>`:
```ts
tooltipElem.text(title);
tooltipElem.html(tooltipElem.html().replace(/&lt;br\/&gt;/g, '<br/>'));
```
This pattern delegates entity encoding to D3 (which handles edge cases correctly) rather than a separate `escapeHtml` implementation. Using `.html()` directly — even after manual escaping — keeps two divergent encoding implementations alive simultaneously and eliminates the need for the private `escapeHtml` method entirely.
